In article <13976@june.cs.washington.edu> pullen@basin.cs.washington.edu (Walter D. Pullen) writes:
>1) New ring: a ring of curse resistance. Wear it and when shamans,
>demons, etc, point at you and curse, or when the air crackles around
>them, you won't be affected. A great plus when fighting the Wiz.
>Perhaps when blessed will protect you against cursed scrolls of
>enchant weapon and enchant armor.
I disagree with this. Most rings protect you against non magic things (cold
fire, etc. ) (it is possible that it is made by magic, but that is irrelevant).
So I think a ring of curse resistance is not very logical. However I like the
idea of some protection against curse.

Maybe the curses should be much more advanced. The shaman points at you and
you get the curse of losing hitpoints. And than you will lose every 100 moves
5 hitpoints (not very bad, but if you have more than one ....). And it should
also be possible to list the curses and blessings:

	Your curses:
		Losing hitpoints
		Gain experience block
		Amnesia
	Your blessings:
		Clairvoyance

You can of course remove the curses with a scroll of remove curse (when it is
cursed you will lose your blessings, when it is uncursed you lose both curses
and blessings and when it is blessed you will only lose your curses). It should
be also possible to use a potion of holy water.

The difference with hallucination and booze is that curses and blessing are for
ever and from potions your body can recover. So clairvoyance should not
disappear after a while, however the most stupid shaman or wizard can remove
that blessing.

